{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-277249",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the roots of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{3x+15}-3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{3x+15}-3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{3x+15} & =3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[4]{3x+15})^{4} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ 3x+15 & =81 \\\\ 3x & =66 \\\\ x & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{3\\cdot 22+15}-3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{81}-3 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=22.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
